186045417] [17592186195003 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "a1b3d5a1-53cc-5f06-95eb-a7eb9be06bd8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186195004 #edb/ref 1080 "$a$ is even" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186195004 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186195004 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5972060e-2639-5856-9e1b-c4bd686c6679" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186195005 #edb/ref 1080 "$a$ is odd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186195005 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186195005 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6aaa509a-629b-5ee8-9e88-255444a14e9f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198105 #edb/ref 1069 "e-12734" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198105 #edb/ref 1071 "$\\qquad$ $x$ is prime and $y$ divides $12$.\n\nWhat is the negation of the composite predicate above?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198105 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5b1d6912-85f0-5ac1-affb-6809d4525f29" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198105 #edb/ref 1074 "De Morgan's law for conjunctions states that\n\n$$\n\\neg (A \\land B) = \\neg A \\lor \\neg B\n$$\n\nSo, the negation of \"$x$ is prime and $y$ divides $12$\" is\n\n$$\n¬(xis prime andydivides12) \\mid ≡¬(xis prime∧ydivides12); ≡¬(xis prime)∨¬(ydivides12); ≡xis not prime∨ydoes not divide12; ≡xis not primeorydoes not divide12\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198113 #edb/ref 1069 "e-12885" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198113 #edb/ref 1071 "$\\qquad$ $x$ is greater than $4$, or $x$ is irrational.\n\nExpress the compound predicate above in symbolic form given the following predicates:\n\n- $P(x)$: $x$ is greater than $4$\n- $Q(x)$: $x$ is rational" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198113 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4402b53e-3c80-5788-b727-20941348c03f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198113 #edb/ref 1074 "The sentence\n\n$\\qquad$ $x$ is irrational\n\ncan be expressed in symbolic form as $\\lnot Q$.\n\nTherefore, the given sentence is expressed symbolically as\n$P\\lor \\lnot Q$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198114 #edb/ref 1069 "e-12886" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198114 #edb/ref 1071 "$\\qquad$ $x$ is a multiple of $5$ or $y$ divides $24$.\n\nWhat is the negation of the composite predicate above?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198114 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ed229458-dba0-5d6b-b32a-b70b253bc1f4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198114 #edb/ref 1074 "De Morgan's law for disjunctions states that\n\n$$\n\\neg (A \\lor B) = \\neg A \\land \\neg B\n$$\n\nSo, the negation of \"$x$ is a multiple of $5$ or $y$ divides $24$\" is\n\n$$\n¬(xis a multiple of [math]5[/math] orydivides24) \\mid ≡¬(xis a multiple of5∨ydivides24); ≡¬(xis a multiple of5)∧¬(ydivides24); ≡xis not a multiple of5∧ydoes not divide24; ≡xis not a multiple of5andydoes not divide24\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198256 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048378 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198256 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049170 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198256 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049546 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198256 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186198695 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198256 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186198696 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198256 #edb/ref 1039 "Expressing a Predicate in Symbolic Form" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198256 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186198113 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198256 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "391d581f-9a2a-5de6-afbe-897917a9f6e3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198257 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186198725 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198257 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186198726 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198257 #edb/ref 1039 "Negating a Conjunction Using De Morgan's Law" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198257 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186198105 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198257 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "28cb0c9e-bf5a-5cab-9147-77e827e21bb2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198258 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186198727 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198258 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186198728 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198258 #edb/ref 1039 "Negating a Disjunction Using De Morgan's Law" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198258 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186198114 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198258 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "c65d0713-5b7a-5559-bef7-7b238edc29ab" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198518 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186199047 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198518 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186199048 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198518 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186199049 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198518 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186199050 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198518 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198518 #edb/ref 1045 "Simplifying Predicate Expressions Using De Morgan's Laws" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198518 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186199047 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198518 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050747 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198518 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "f34a1f9e-dc25-5a56-b69f-2cc175647229" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198696 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186194802 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198696 #edb/ref 1069 "q-170806" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198696 #edb/ref 1071 "$x$ is not both positive and an integer.\n\nExpress the compound predicate above in symbolic form given the following predicates:\n\n- $P(x)$: $x$ is positive\n- $Q(x)$: $x$ is integer" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198696 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e716194e-3ab1-59dd-b4e2-2926a9bd85ac" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198727 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186194997 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198727 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186195000 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198727 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186195003 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198727 #edb/ref 1069 "q-175329" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198727 #edb/ref 1071 "$a$ is even or $b$ is odd.\n\nThe negation of the composite predicate above is the following:\n\n{{field-1}} {{field-2}} {{field-3}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198727 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "078171ae-79c8-5810-aaf2-bebda0bbeadd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199047 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186199048 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199047 #edb/ref 1061 143820 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199047 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "d42da4d8-71de-5617-a193-de6538fc1c98" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199047 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186199524 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199048 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186199049 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199048 #edb/ref 1061 143821 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199048 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "039cf98e-03ec-569f-b5a1-bd97dbc07419" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199048 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186198256 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199049 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186199050 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199049 #edb/ref 1061 143824 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199049 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "c2a6fe5e-56b3-5f92-9b04-22194ce9fabd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199049 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186198257 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199050 #edb/ref 1061 143827 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199050 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "1c572864-399d-5930-9178-c0590397d869" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199050 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186198258 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199524 #edb/ref 1064 "Logical operations with predicates generalize the corresponding operations on statements. As a result, all the properties of these operations are held.\n\nIn particular, for predicates $P(x_1,x_2\\ldots,x_n)$ and $Q(y_1,y_2\\ldots,y_m)$, De Morgan's laws state the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}¬(P∧Q) & ≡¬P∨¬Q \\\\ ¬(P∨Q) & ≡¬P∧¬Q\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThese can be used to negate open sentences containing conjunctions and disjunctions. For example, let's negate the following:\n\n$$\nn \\ge 0 \\:\\textbf{or}\\: 2 \\mid m\n$$\n\nApplying De Morgan's law for disjunctions, we obtain\n\n$$\n¬(n \\ge 0or2∣m) \\mid ≡¬(n \\ge 0∨2∣m); ≡¬(n \\ge 0)∧¬(2∣m); ≡n < 0∧2∤m; ≡n < 0and2∤m\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199524 #edb/ref 1065 7990 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199524 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "476f8b41-cb95-5623-94e3-dc7a863c3df5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199524 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
